    "diagnosis": "Familial adenomatous polyposis",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Gastric foveolar-type adenoma. The vast majority of gastric adenomas in familial adenomatous polyposis are foveolar-type adenomas with low-grade dysplasia, mainly located in the gastric body; distinction between a fundic gland polyp with low-grade dysplasia and a gastric foveolar-type adenoma can be difficult, but this is of little importance because the risk of neoplastic progression is very low for both lesions.",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Brosens LAA",
