    "legend": "Gastric intestinal-type adenomas. These polyps are rare and seem to be related to <em>Helicobacter pylori</em> infection and chronic atrophic gastritis; detection of <em>H. pylori</em> infection, gastric atrophy, and intestinal-type adenomas in patients with familial adenomatous polyposis seem to be important to identify patients at increased risk of gastric cancer.",
