    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong>Table&nbsp;2.22</strong> Summary of the main features of familial adenomatous polyposis</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Arends MJ and Frayling I.",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 694.5pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"926\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Feature</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 481.9pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"643\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Syndrome characteristics</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Syndrome MIM number(s)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 481.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"643\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">175100</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Associated malignant tumours</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 481.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"643\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Colorectal cancer, duodenal&nbsp;/ small intestinal cancer, gastric cancer, desmoid tumour&nbsp;/ fibromatosis, hepatoblastoma, thyroid cancer, biliary tree cancer, pancreas cancer, CNS cancer including medulloblastoma, adrenocortical cancer</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Associated benign tumours</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 481.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"643\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Colorectal adenoma, duodenal&nbsp;/ small intestinal adenoma, gastric adenoma, gastric fundic gland polyp, adrenocortical adenoma, osteoma, odontoma, epidermoid cyst</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Cancer-related inheritance</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 481.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"643\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Autosomal dominant</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Chromosome location</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 481.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"643\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>APC</em> (5q22.2)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Protein product&ndash;associated pathway</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 481.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"643\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">WNT pathway: APC is a regulator of the WNT signalling pathway that acts as a key scaffold protein binding critical components (including AXIN2 and phosphorylating enzymes) that tag (by phosphorylation and subsequently ubiquitination) the WNT effector protein &beta;-catenin for proteasomal destruction</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
